      <p>Melissa Fisher is an award-winning director, writer, and multi-hyphenate in the industry. Her directorial work marries poetic imagery and technical craft to create emotionally evocative drama. She is an alumni of the 2026 <strong>AFI DWW+</strong> and a member of the International Cinematographer's Guild with over 15 years of experience on the sets of <strong>Academy</strong> and <strong>Emmy Award-winning</strong> films and television series.</p>
      <p>Fisher graduated from Chapman University’s Dodge College of Film and Media Arts with a BFA in Film Production. She worked her way up from a camera PA on <strong>Michael Bay’s <em>PAIN &amp; GAIN</em></strong> to camera assist on films like <strong>Damien Chazelle’s <em>LA LA LAND</em></strong> and <strong><em>FIRST MAN</em></strong>, to eventually running the camera department on hit television shows like <strong><em>GLOW</em> (Netflix)</strong> and <strong><em>THE DROPOUT (Hulu)</em></strong>. Her experience behind the camera has given her a keen sense for aesthetic visual storytelling.</p>
      <p>Fisher is drawn to projects that tackle social justice themes and highlight marginalized communities. Her most recent short film <strong><em>INSIDE THESE WALLS</em></strong> was chosen as a finalist for the Pandora Short Film Grant, and stars Isabella Briggs (<strong><em>THE SUMMER I TURNED PRETTY</em></strong>) and Bobby Soto (<strong><em>THE TAX COLLECTOR</em></strong>). The film centers around a young family navigating the U.S. prison system, and premiered at the Oscar-qualifying deadCenter Film Festival.</p>
      <p>Fisher’s previous film <strong><em>BUSCANDO ALMA</em></strong> focused on immigration and gender identity, and won numerous awards around the world including the <strong>Oscar-qualifying Jury Award</strong> at Atlanta’s Out On Film Festival making it eligible for the <strong>2025 Academy Awards</strong>.</p>
      <p>Fisher has shadowed on the <strong>Amazon Prime</strong> series <strong><em>BALLARD</em></strong>, and is currently developing her debut feature film <strong><em>IN THE WAKE OF YOUTH</em></strong>.</p>
